1
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:23,254
Volcan, built for Alexa+, lets blind and low-vision developers review AI code by voice.

2
00:00:23,254 --> 00:01:25,795
Press once, and this patch goes to Amazon Bedrock.

3
00:01:25,795 --> 00:01:34,061
Amazon Bedrock answered Volcan on AWS Lambda, with DynamoDB. That's how much it read.

4
00:01:34,061 --> 00:02:05,530
Request changes stages a review, bound to the head commit it read.

5
00:02:05,530 --> 00:02:34,813
Nothing leaves Volcan until you confirm. Confirm, and listen.

6
00:02:34,813 --> 00:02:39,179
No GitHub token here: the request is recorded, not sent.

7
00:02:39,179 --> 00:02:45,308
This MCP handshake is real. Alexa+ never called Volcan.
